<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">German South West Africa</h1><p class="st-meta">1884 CE – 1915 CE · capital Windhoek</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Germany's colony in Namibia, a settler territory where the colonial army committed genocide against the Herero and Nama.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1883 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/free-hanseatic-city-of-bremen">Bremen</a> merchant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-luderitz">Adolf Lüderitz</a> bought land at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luderitz">Angra Pequena</a>, and on 24 April 1884 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> declared a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. Protection treaties with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/herero-paramountcy">Herero Paramountcy</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rehoboth-basters">Rehoboth Basters</a> followed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/curt-von-francois">Curt von François</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/windhoek">Windhoek</a> as the capital in 1890.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodor-leutwein">Theodor Leutwein</a> ruled through treaties with chiefs while settlers took land and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herero-people">Herero</a> rising of 1904 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nama-people">Nama</a> war under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hendrik-witbooi">Hendrik Witbooi</a> were crushed by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothar-von-trotha">Lothar von Trotha</a>; tens of thousands died in the desert and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camps</a> such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shark-island-concentration-camp">Shark Island</a>. Diamonds found near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luderitz">Lüderitz</a> in 1908 made the colony profitable.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>South African forces invaded during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, and the German garrison surrendered at Khorab in July 1915. The territory became <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/south-west-africa">South West Africa</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> formally acknowledged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> in 2021.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/german-south-west-africa.jpg" alt="German South West Africa" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Imperial Colonial Office of the German Empire Vector: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reichskolonialflagge.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1884 CE – 1915 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Windhoek</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Theodor Leutwein, Lothar von Trotha</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity, traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Otjiherero, Khoekhoe, Oshiwambo</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/namibia">Namibia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Deutsch-Sudwestafrika</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1900&amp;focus=german-south-west-africa" aria-label="German South West Africa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5137 3011 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where German South West Africa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5457 3267L5434 3101M5457 3267L5489 3158M5457 3267L5454 3246M5457 3267L5471 3358M5457 3267L5490 3475M5457 3267L5456 3293M5457 3267L5300 622M5457 3267L5457 3267"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5434 3101h0M5489 3158h0M5454 3246h0M5471 3358h0M5490 3475h0M5456 3293h0M5300 622h0M5457 3267h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5457 3267h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5457 3267h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Windhoek. <a href="/atlas?year=1900&amp;focus=german-south-west-africa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
